WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.900
A sunny winter morning on the bridge. The icicle on the lantern begins to drip.

2
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:11.650
In this particle model, ice has an open pattern. Energy entering can melt it.

3
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:15.900
The same water molecules move past their neighbors. The sample stays at 0 °C while ice melts.

4
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:22.900
Melt the ice in a sealed jar on a balance. The balance does not move: same particles, same mass.

5
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:29.900
Energy leaves the jar’s water. Its molecules return to the open ice pattern and still vibrate.

6
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Melting and freezing rearrange the same water molecules. No new substance is made. (Model.)
